        "slot": "s1",
        "stem": "Which option best combines these two sentences into one correct sentence? “The library extended its evening hours. Many students needed a quiet place to study.”",
        "options": [
          {
            "text": "The library extended its evening hours because many students needed a quiet place to study.",
            "isKey": true,
            "misconception": null,
            "rationale": "This sentence clearly shows that students’ need for study space was the reason for the longer hours."
          },
          {
            "text": "The library extended its evening hours, many students needed a quiet place to study.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "COMMA_SPLICE",
            "rationale": "This joins two complete sentences with only a comma, which creates a comma splice."
          },
          {
            "text": "The library extended its evening hours although many students needed a quiet place to study.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "MISUSES_CONTRAST_LINKER",
            "rationale": "Although signals an unexpected contrast, but the two ideas show a reason and result."
          },
          {
            "text": "The library extended its evening hours, needing many students a quiet place to study.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "UNCLEAR_MODIFIER",
            "rationale": "The phrase suggests that the library needed students, so the meaning is unclear."
          }
        ],
        "evidenceQuote": null
